Billy Coven <hostilnakfor@yahoo.com> wrote:
>The player and the monsters often have disjoint speed values.
>Couldn't this be abused so that every time the monster is about to
>attack, the adventurer steps backwards?

Not with complete reliability, because if you are faster than speed 12,
your movement ration received each game tick fluctuates:

   If you are fast, then you will get 12 movement points every turn,
   and a 2/3 random chance of receiving another 6. (Average speed: 16)

   If you are very fast, then you will get 18 movement points every
   turn, and a 1/3 random chance of receiving another 6. (Average speed:
   20).

Some monsters are speed 20 or faster; quite a few are speed 16 or
faster.

